    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759-a1">

                <pb facs="0916" n="822" xml:id="pg822"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No
                    2756.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr. Pulido.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1896</hi>. (<hi
                                rendition="#italic">1895?</hi>)</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: My Government being desirous of
                    obtaining an authenticated copy of the record of the trial of Mr. Julio
                    Sanguily, an American citizen, on the charge of rebellion, instructs me to ask
                    for it; therefore I beg your excellency to please order that a copy be furnished
                    me for the purpose aforesaid.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O. Williams</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
